WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.822
Most everyday Pandas work can be organized into a compact sequence.

00:00:04.822 --> 00:00:09.777
Load the data. Profile it using head, shape, and info.

00:00:09.777 --> 00:00:17.352
Clean values using type conversion, missing-value handling, duplicate checks, and string methods.

00:00:17.352 --> 00:00:19.422
Select the rows you need.

00:00:19.422 --> 00:00:25.067
Create useful transformations. Summarize with groupby and pivot tables.

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:30.793
Combine tables when necessary. Then validate row counts, keys, and totals.

00:00:31.394 --> 00:00:38.636
You do not need to memorize hundreds of functions if you understand this workflow and know how to consult documentation.

00:00:38.636 --> 00:00:42.546
Also remember that Pandas is not always the right tool.

00:00:42.546 --> 00:00:48.326
Very large datasets may be better processed in SQL, Spark, Polars,

00:00:48.326 --> 00:00:51.899
or another system designed for larger-scale computation.
